                    { 'Key Item Silver-labeled vial' },
                    { 'Key Item Gold-labeled vial.' },
                } },
            } },
            { 'Return to Miageau (A) to complete the quest.' },
        },
    },
    ['Wayward Wares'] = {
        title             = 'Wayward Wares',
        starting_npc      = 'Chapi Galepilai (A) (G-10), Abyssea - Attohwa',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'A shipment of essential supplies intended for the Resistance outpost has been intercepted. Recover the scattered materials and deliver them to their intended destination.',
        required_fame     = 'Abyssea - Attohwa Fame Level: 1',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Abyssea',
        rewards           = 'Based on how many Key Item returned: Varying amount of Cruor: 100~400 Varying amount of Resistance Credits: 25~100',
        previous_quest    = 'None',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak with Chapi Galepilai (A) (G-10), Abyssea - Attohwa.' },
            { 'You will be asked to retrieve missing supplies. There are three total.' },
            { 'All three supply packs are around the Crevice Amoeban / Treacle Slugs:', sub = {
                { 'Key Item Pulse martello repair pack (G-8)' },
                { 'Key Item Clone ward reinforcement pack (F-9)' },
                { 'Key Item Pack of outpost repair tools (F-9)' },
            } },
            { 'Once you have found at least one of the packs, speak to Morlepiche (A) at Veridical Conflux #00 to complete the quest.' },
        },
    },
    ['Weapons, Not Worries'] = {
        title             = 'Weapons, Not Worries',
        starting_npc      = 'Peshi Yohnts (A) (F-9), Abyssea - Tahrongi',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'Yes',
        description       = 'A down-in-the-dumps artisan, seemingly too disheartened to take action herself, needs you to retrieve supplies for weaponcrafting. The hardened bone harvestable in the area should serve to raise her spirits.',
        required_fame     = 'Abyssea - Tahrongi Fame Level: 1',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Abyssea',
        requirements      = 'Pickaxe Hardened Bone',
        rewards           = '100 Cruor',
        previous_quest    = 'None',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak to Peshi Yohnts (A) at (F-9) in the Western Encampment. Veridical Conflux #03 is nearby.', sub = {
                { 'You\'ll need to speak to Kupipi (A) at (H-12) beforehand if you\'ve never done so before.' },
            } },
            { 'She\'ll give you a Pickaxe and asks you to excavate a Hardened Bone from Excavation Points, or purchased on the Auction House.', sub = {
                { 'She\'ll only give you one so any extras from failure or repeating the quest will require your to bring own.' },
            } },
            { 'Excavation Points are located at (E-5), scattered around the dragon skeleton. This is a little walk from Veridical Conflux #06.', sub = {
                { 'Mine until you find a Hardened Bone; multiple bones can be mined in a single session.' },
                { 'Various other junk can be obtained rather than the Hardened Bone. There is a respawn timer on the Excavation Points.' },
            } },
            { 'Trade Peshi Yohnts (A) a Hardened Bone to complete the quest.', sub = {
                { 'Note as soon as you engage her to repeat the quest a second time, it automatically is flagged in the quest log.' },
                { '50 quest completions will max fame in this zone.' },
            } },
        },
    },
    ['When Good Cardians Go Bad'] = {
        title             = 'When Good Cardians Go Bad',
        starting_npc      = 'Apururu (A) (H-12), Abyssea - Tahrongi',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'Yes',
        description       = 'Apururu\'s Cardians now guard each encampment, but word has it that not all of them are functioning optimally. Speak to the Cardians at each location and report back on any glitches you may have detected.',
        required_fame     = 'Abyssea - Tahrongi Fame Level: 4',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Abyssea',
        rewards           = 'First time completion: Key Item Viridian abyssite of guerdon Subsequent completions: 400 Cruor',
        previous_quest    = 'His Box, His Beloved',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        note              = 'Zoning resets progress on this quest. Travel around to the five cardians (2 to 6 of Diamonds) Two guard the main camp (at each exit) One is at each of the other three encampments (Conflux #03, #05, and #07) Some, or all, of the Cardians will give odd responses. They\'re generally pretty blatant, just pay attention to what they\'re saying. Be careful, as one incorrect word might be all that is wrong with a cardian\'s message. It is easy to miss with the way they talk. Additionally, they may have correct responses but if they speak with hollow stars (☆), that response is still incorrect. Report which Cardians gave the odd responses to Apururu (A) to complete the quest. You must choose perfect answers or the quest will not be completed. If you fail, zone to retry. Zoning is required to repeat this quest.  Retrieved from "https://www.bg-wiki.com/index.php?title=When_Good_Cardians_Go_Bad&oldid=641199" window[\'nitroAds\'].createAd(\'bgwiki-anchor\', { "refreshLimit": 0, "refreshTime": 30, "format": "anchor", "anchor": "bottom", "report": { "enabled": true, "icon": true, "wording": "Report Ad", "position": "top-right" },  "mediaQuery": "(min-width: 0px)" }); window[\'nitroAds\'].createAd(\'nitro-video\', { "refreshTime": 30, "format": "floating", "report": { "enabled": true, "icon": true, "wording": "Report Ad", "position": "top-left" } }); Categories: QuestsAbyssea QuestsAbyssea - Tahrongi QuestsRepeatable QuestsFFXI Wiki',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Talk to Apururu (A) at (H-12).', sub = {
                { 'Note: Zoning resets progress on this quest.' },
            } },
            { 'Travel around to the five cardians (2 to 6 of Diamonds)', sub = {
                { 'Two guard the main camp (at each exit)' },
                { 'One is at each of the other three encampments (Conflux #03, #05, and #07)' },
            } },
            { 'Some, or all, of the Cardians will give odd responses. They\'re generally pretty blatant, just pay attention to what they\'re saying.', sub = {
                { 'Be careful, as one incorrect word might be all that is wrong with a cardian\'s message. It is easy to miss with the way they talk.' },
                { 'Additionally, they may have correct responses but if they speak with hollow stars (☆), that response is still incorrect.' },
            } },
            { 'Report which Cardians gave the odd responses to Apururu (A) to complete the quest.', sub = {
                { 'You must choose perfect answers or the quest will not be completed. If you fail, zone to retry.' },
            } },
        },
    },
    ['Whither the Whisker'] = {
        title             = 'Whither the Whisker',
        starting_npc      = 'Rahal (A) (F-4), Abyssea - Vunkerl',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'A savage pack of fiends terrorizes Vunkerl, their whisker of power and omniscience confounding the bravest attempts of a celebrated San d\'Orian hero to secure the safety of his men. It falls to you to sever and retrieve this Samsonian strand!',
        required_fame     = 'Abyssea Fame Level: 3',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Abyssea',
        requirements      = 'Black Whisker',
        rewards           = '800 Cruor, Key Item Crimson abyssite of celerity',
        previous_quest    = 'None',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak to Rahal (A) at (F-4).' },
            { 'Procure a Black Whisker, which drops from Slaughterous Smilodons or can be purchased on the Auction House.', sub = {
                { 'They are located north of Veridical Conflux #04.' },
            } },
            { 'Trade the Black Whisker to Rahal (A) to complete the quest.' },
        },
    },
}

quest_info['adoulin'] = {
    ['"Always more," Quoth the Ravenous'] = {
        title             = '"Always more," Quoth the Ravenous',
        starting_npc      = 'Westerly Breeze, Western Adoulin - (I-5)',
        subtitle          = 'Friend to Gluttons',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'The third time may be a charm for some things, but the infamous starving Couriers\' Coalition member brings only bad tidings--this time in the form of a sparkling pink beverage. Will it be his last request ever?',
        required_fame     = 'Adoulin Fame Level: 3',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Seekers of Adoulin',
        requirements      = 'Cursed Beverage',
        rewards           = '1500 Experience Points 1000 Bayld',
        previous_quest    = 'The Starving',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak to Westerly Breeze at (I-5) in Western Adoulin (you must zone and wait until the following game day after completing the previous quest).' },
            { 'Trade him a Cursed Beverage to him to complete the quest.' },
        },
    },
    ['A Barrel of Laughs'] = {
        title             = 'A Barrel of Laughs',
        starting_npc      = 'Tuffle-Buffle, Western Adoulin',
        subtitle          = 'Sauce Supreme',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'A mannequin of curious origins has been wrested from Tarutaru Sauce\'s control. The suspects are not altogether unknown, and the prize can\'t be far. Search the immediate area for traces of its whereabouts.',
        required_fame     = 'Adoulin Fame Level: Unknown',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Seekers of Adoulin',
        rewards           = '1000 Experience Points One of the following: Anastasi Earring Burana Earring Gelos Earring Hija Earring',
        previous_quest    = 'To Laugh Is to Love',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'You need to wait until the day changes after completing the previous quest.' },
            { 'Examine the Mischief Marker at (J-11) in Western Adoulin for a cutscene.' },
            { 'To the left of the Mischief Marker is a door marked (Door: Depository), examine it for a cutscene.' },
            { 'Travel to Rala Waterways (M-6) from Eastern Adoulin (F-7) (Peacekeepers Warp) and examine the door behind Yeggha Dolashi for a cutscene.' },
            { 'Examine the door again to enter a battlefield against the Dashing Dreamers: Celestin (BLU), Fabioso (RDM), and their Mithra mannequin (RDM)', sub = {
                { 'Only the enemy mannequin (Pupadi Dollmohr) needs to be defeated to clear the battlefield.', sub = {
                    { 'The mannequin only has about 55,000 HP.' },
                    { 'Fabioso can cast Charm.' },
                } },
                { 'You will be assisted by the Tarutaru Sauce duo Tuffle-Buffle (BLM) and Musto-Rusto (RDM)', sub = {
                    { 'The Tarutaru duo is relatively frail but will remain at a distance if enemies are held far.' },
                } },
                { 'If either of your Tarutaru allies are defeated, you will instantly lose and be ejected from the fight.' },
                { 'If you fail, head to the Waterfront in Western Adoulin and click the Sauce Barrels (found on end of pier next to Jorin) for a cutscene demanding a specific food item from one of the vendors in town.' },
                { 'Return to the Sauce Barrels with the demanded food item and trade it to them.' },
                { 'Upon giving them the demanded food, you may return to the arena in Rala Waterways and retry the battlefield.' },
            } },
        },
    },
    ['A Certain Substitute Patrolman'] = {
        title             = 'A Certain Substitute Patrolman',
        starting_npc      = 'Rising Solstice, Western Adoulin - (D-9)',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'The soldier charged with making the rounds in Western Adoulin has fallen not ill, but asleep. Do the Peacekeepers\' Coalition a service by filling in for him and following his assigned route to the letter.',
        required_fame     = 'Adoulin Fame Level: 1',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Seekers of Adoulin',
        rewards           = '1000 Experience Points 500 Bayld',
        previous_quest    = 'None',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak to Rising Solstice in Western Adoulin (D-9) to accept the quest and obtain the Western Adoulin patrol route Temporary Key Item.' },
            { 'Speak to the following NPCs in Western Adoulin in order. You may use Waypoints to expedite the process.', sub = {
                { 'Pioneer\'s Coalition: Zaoso (E-8)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to him until he repeats: "I welcome you with open arms to the Pioneer\'s Coalition!"' },
                } },
                { 'Courier\'s Coalition: Clemmar (G-8)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to him until he repeats: "What can the Courier\'s do for you?..."' },
                } },
                { 'Waterfront (near the Geomancer Sylvie): Kongramm (I-5)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to him until he repeats: "Good Work. Everything\'s in order. Now shove it."' },
                } },
                { 'Platea Triumphus (Water Fountain): Virsaint (H-8)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to him until he repeats "The leaders of the six coalitions are all termed "maesters"..."' },
                } },
                { 'Inventors\' Coalition: Shipilolo (J-9)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to her until she repeats "If you came here seeking the brightaruest minds of all in Adoulin, then you\'re in luck!"' },
                } },
                { 'Rent-a-room Entrance: Dangueubert (H-11)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to him until he prompts you with the Mog Garden Menu' },
                } },
                { 'Mummers\' Coalition: Nylene (H-10)', sub = {
                    { 'Talk to her until she repeats: "If you\'re a fun-loving lord/lady looking for a good time..."' },
                } },
            } },
            { 'Return to Rising Solstice for your reward.' },
        },
    },
    ['A Geothermal Expedition'] = {
        title             = 'A Geothermal Expedition',
        starting_npc      = 'Fallion, Morimar Basalt Fields - (I-10)',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'Hot springs are not only good for relaxation--they are also worth researching! Test the water of hot springs in different locations throughout Morimar Basalt Fields and summarize your findings.',
        required_fame     = 'Adoulin Fame Level: Unknown',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Seekers of Adoulin',
        rewards           = '3000 Experience Points 300 Bayld',
        previous_quest    = 'None',
        next_quest        = 'None',
        walkthrough       = {
            { 'Speak with Fallion (I-10) to initiate the quest (Bivouac #3).' },
            { 'Visit and test the three Hot Springs, under different conditions, to obtain 5 reports.', sub = {
                { 'Hot Spring locations are: H-7, G-8 and H-8.' },
                { 'Easiest to start at (Bivouac #2) and go south.' },
                { 'There is no weather requirement for the reports. They seem to be based purely on time.', sub = {
